LITS Patent Non-Assertion Covenant
===================================

Canonical text of the covenant summarised in GOVERNANCE.md §3. Its purpose is to let any
party — including a competitor — invest in implementing the LITS contract without fear of a
patent ambush, and to signal to the State and to other vendors that the standard is genuinely
open.

1. Definitions
--------------
"Contract" means the published LITS API contract in this repository: openapi.yaml,
openapi-admin.yaml, and the normative schemas and examples they reference.

"Conformant Implementation" means software, to the extent it implements the Contract and passes
the conformance suite in reference-impl/tests/.

"Necessary Claims" means those patent claims that the Steward or a Contributor owns or controls
and that are necessarily infringed by implementing the Contract, where there is no commercially
reasonable, non-infringing alternative way to implement it. Necessary Claims do NOT include
claims infringed only because of: (a) features or functions not required by the Contract, or
(b) combination of a Conformant Implementation with other software or hardware.

"Steward" means the current steward of the Contract (see GOVERNANCE.md §2); "Contributor" means
any party that contributes to the Contract.

2. The covenant
---------------
The Steward and each Contributor irrevocably covenant not to assert any Necessary Claims against
any party for making, using, selling, offering, importing, or operating a Conformant
Implementation, for as long as that implementation remains conformant.

3. Defensive suspension
-----------------------
The covenant extended to a given party is suspended if that party (or its affiliate) initiates or
voluntarily participates in a patent assertion (a claim, cross-claim, or counterclaim) alleging
that the Contract or any Conformant Implementation infringes a patent. This protects good-faith
implementers without disarming the ecosystem against an aggressor.

4. Relationship to the Apache License 2.0
-----------------------------------------
This covenant is IN ADDITION TO, and does not limit, the patent licence granted under the Apache
License 2.0 (see LICENSE) for code contributed to this repository. Where the two overlap, the
broader grant controls.

5. Scope limits
---------------
This covenant grants no rights under copyright, and no trademark rights. Copyright licensing is in
LICENSE and LICENSE-docs; trademark and conformance-mark terms are in TRADEMARK.md.

6. Durability
-------------
The covenant is irrevocable (subject only to §3) and SURVIVES any transfer of stewardship,
including the handover of the Contract to the State or a neutral national body on designation
(GOVERNANCE.md §2). Consistent with GOVERNANCE.md §7, it is a one-way ratchet: a future steward
may broaden it but may not revoke or narrow it.

